      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KHABALOV (1) is knocking on the door and sets up well for this, having run third in a CL4 at this track last start after jumping awkwardly and racing keenly, then missing by less than a length as favourite. His Townsville second in CL5 two back adds depth, and his record at this track and distance gives him the right platform. SMART MISSION (2) is the clear danger after being checked and beaten a nose first-up at Townsville, with the return to 1250m a genuine positive given his distance record. DEEP STEALTH (8) resumes for a new yard and brings consistent northern NSW form, including a BM66 placing at Ballina on heavy ground and a sound CL2 fourth at Grafton. KIRKALL (4) comes off a break after ending last campaign with a BM65 win at Oak Park and a BM55 second at Townsville. Holds genuine appeal if he can pick up from where he left off. TIPPED OFF (3) was better last time here when doing his best work late. If the pace is strong he could cause a late scare.",
